/-!
# Normal subgroups of K-groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 11.128)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.128 (M. Emaldi): a group `G` is a
`K`-group if every subgroup `A` has a subgroup `B` with `A ∩ B = 1` and `⟨A, B⟩ = G`. Are normal
subgroups of `K`-groups also `K`-groups?

The theorem `normalSubgroupOfKGroupIsKGroup_refuted` gives a counterexample.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.128 (M.
Emaldi). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700820 (`KOU-11.128`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`A ∩ B = 1` and `⟨A, B⟩ = G` are `A ⊓ B = ⊥` and `A ⊔ B = ⊤` in the subgroup lattice, that is
`IsCompl A B`, so a `K`-group is a group whose subgroup lattice is complemented: Mathlib's
`ComplementedLattice (Subgroup G)`. Groups are in `Type`.

## Construction

Let `X` be the countable product of copies of the group of order two. It acts on the direct sum
`P` of copies of the group of order three by changing signs independently. In the semidirect
product `H = P ⋊ X`, the invariant subgroup generated by any part of `P` is the direct sum of
its active coordinates. The remaining coordinates and a complement in `X` supply a lattice
complement in `H`.

Let `W` be the functions from `X` to the field of seven elements that depend on finitely many
coordinates. Translations by `X` permute the cells with a given prefix length. The generator of
`P` at coordinate `i` multiplies a function by 2 or 4 according to the value of that coordinate.
These two eigenvalues allow projection onto either half of the cube. Thus the orbit of any nonzero
function spans all of `W`, and `G = W ⋊ H` has a complemented subgroup lattice.

In the normal subgroup `N = W ⋊ P`, consider the functions vanishing at zero. A complement would
give a subspace on which evaluation at zero is injective and which contains a function `f` with
`f 0 = 1`. Project `f` onto the half where a fresh coordinate equals one. The projection vanishes at
zero and still takes the value one at the point obtained by flipping that coordinate.
-/

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ComplementedSubgroupLatticeNormalKourovka11Problem128Wanted

/-- **Kourovka Problem 11.128 on normal subgroups of $K$-groups.** Call a group $G$ a $K$-group
when its subgroup lattice is complemented: every subgroup $A$ of $G$ has a subgroup $B$ with
$A \cap B = 1$ and $\langle A, B \rangle = G$. This is the assertion (M. Emaldi) that every normal
subgroup of a $K$-group, viewed as a group in its own right, is again a $K$-group. -/
@[expose] public def normalSubgroupOfKGroupIsKGroup : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], ComplementedLattice (Subgroup G) → ∀ N : Subgroup G, N.Normal →
    ComplementedLattice (Subgroup N)

open SemidirectProduct Multiplicative

/-! ### Complements in split extensions with abelian kernel -/

private abbrev Stable {V H : Type} [Group V] [Group H] (φ : H →* MulAut V)
    (S : Subgroup V) := ∀ h, ∀ v ∈ S, φ h v ∈ S

private theorem conj_inl {V H : Type} [CommGroup V] [Group H] {φ : H →* MulAut V}
    (g : V ⋊[φ] H) (v : V) : g * inl v * g⁻¹ = inl (φ g.right v) := by
  ext <;> simp [mul_comm]

-- A subgroup projecting onto the acting group acts on the abelian kernel by the full action.
private theorem stable_comap {V H : Type} [CommGroup V] [Group H] {φ : H →* MulAut V}
    (J : Subgroup (V ⋊[φ] H)) (hj : J.map rightHom = ⊤) : Stable φ (J.comap inl) := by
  intro h v hv
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hg'⟩ := Subgroup.mem_map.mp (hj.ge (Subgroup.mem_top h))
  change inl (φ h v) ∈ J
  change g.right = h at hg'
  rw [← hg', ← conj_inl g]
  exact J.mul_mem (J.mul_mem hg hv) (J.inv_mem hg)

private def pairSubgroup {V H : Type} [Group V] [Group H] {φ : H →* MulAut V}
    (L : Subgroup V) (hL : Stable φ L) (C : Subgroup H) : Subgroup (V ⋊[φ] H) where
  carrier := {g | g.left ∈ L ∧ g.right ∈ C}
  one_mem' := ⟨L.one_mem, C.one_mem⟩
  mul_mem' := fun ha hb ↦ ⟨L.mul_mem ha.1 (hL _ _ hb.1), C.mul_mem ha.2 hb.2⟩
  inv_mem' := fun ha ↦ ⟨hL _ _ (L.inv_mem ha.1), C.inv_mem ha.2⟩

-- It suffices to complement the invariant subgroup generated by the intersection with the kernel.
private theorem semidirect_complemented {V H : Type} [CommGroup V] [Group H]
    (φ : H →* MulAut V) (hH : ComplementedLattice (Subgroup H))
    (split : ∀ D : Subgroup V, ∃ L : Subgroup V, Stable φ L ∧ Disjoint D L ∧
      ∀ S : Subgroup V, Stable φ S → D ≤ S → L ≤ S → S = ⊤) :
    ComplementedLattice (Subgroup (V ⋊[φ] H)) := by
  constructor
  intro A
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := hH.exists_isCompl (A.map rightHom)
  obtain ⟨L, hL, hd, hgen⟩ := split (A.comap inl)
  let B := pairSubgroup L hL C
  refine ⟨B, ?_, ?_⟩
  · apply Subgroup.disjoint_def.mpr
    intro g ha hb
    obtain ⟨hl, hr⟩ : g.left ∈ L ∧ g.right ∈ C := hb
    have h1 := Subgroup.disjoint_def.mp hC.disjoint (Subgroup.mem_map_of_mem _ ha) hr
    change g.right = 1 at h1
    have he : inl g.left = g := SemidirectProduct.ext rfl h1.symm
    have h2 := Subgroup.disjoint_def.mp hd (show g.left ∈ A.comap inl from he ▸ ha) hl
    exact SemidirectProduct.ext h2 h1
  · apply codisjoint_iff.mpr
    let J := A ⊔ B
    have hj : J.map rightHom = ⊤ := by
      refine top_unique (hC.sup_eq_top.ge.trans ?_)
      apply sup_le (Subgroup.map_mono le_sup_left)
      intro c hc
      exact ⟨inr c, Subgroup.mem_sup_right (show inr c ∈ B from ⟨L.one_mem, hc⟩), rfl⟩
    have hk : J.comap inl = ⊤ := hgen _ (stable_comap J hj)
      (Subgroup.comap_mono le_sup_left)
      (fun v hv ↦ Subgroup.mem_sup_right (show inl v ∈ B from ⟨hv, C.one_mem⟩))
    apply J.eq_top_iff'.mpr
    intro g
    obtain ⟨a, ha, ha'⟩ := Subgroup.mem_map.mp (hj.ge (Subgroup.mem_top g.right))
    have he : inl (g * a⁻¹).left = g * a⁻¹ := by
      change a.right = g.right at ha'
      refine SemidirectProduct.ext rfl ?_
      simp [ha']
    have hm : inl (g * a⁻¹).left ∈ J := hk.ge (Subgroup.mem_top _)
    exact (J.mul_mem_cancel_right (J.inv_mem ha)).mp (he ▸ hm)

private theorem elementary_complemented (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (E : Type) [AddCommGroup E]
    [Module (ZMod p) E] : ComplementedLattice (Subgroup (Multiplicative E)) :=
  ((AddSubgroup.toZModSubmodule p).symm.trans AddSubgroup.toSubgroup).complementedLattice

/-! ### Coordinate sign changes on the direct sum of copies of the group of order three -/

private abbrev X := ℕ → ZMod 2
private abbrev P := ℕ →₀ ZMod 3
private abbrev T := Multiplicative X
private abbrev M := Multiplicative P

private def sgn (b : ZMod 2) : ZMod 3 := if b = 0 then 1 else -1

private theorem sgn_add (a b : ZMod 2) : sgn (a + b) = sgn a * sgn b := by decide +revert

private noncomputable def twist (x : X) (p : P) : P :=
  Finsupp.onFinset p.support (fun i ↦ sgn (x i) * p i) (by
    intro i hi
    contrapose hi
    simp [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp hi])

private def actionOf {E H : Type} [AddGroup E] [Group H] (f : H → E → E)
    (fadd : ∀ h a b, f h (a + b) = f h a + f h b)
    (fid : ∀ a, f 1 a = a) (fmul : ∀ h k a, f (h * k) a = f h (f k a)) :
    H →* MulAut (Multiplicative E) where
  toFun h := AddEquiv.toMultiplicative
    { toFun := f h
      invFun := f h⁻¹
      left_inv := fun a ↦ by rw [← fmul, inv_mul_cancel, fid]
      right_inv := fun a ↦ by rw [← fmul, mul_inv_cancel, fid]
      map_add' := fadd h }
  map_one' := DFunLike.ext _ _ fun a ↦ congrArg (ofAdd : E → Multiplicative E) (fid a.toAdd)
  map_mul' h k := DFunLike.ext _ _ fun a ↦
    congrArg (ofAdd : E → Multiplicative E) (fmul h k a.toAdd)

private noncomputable def flips : T →* MulAut M :=
  actionOf (fun x p ↦ twist x.toAdd p)
    (by intro x a b; ext i; exact mul_add ..)
    (by intro a; ext i; exact one_mul _)
    (by intro x y a; ext i; exact (congrArg (· * a i) (sgn_add _ _)).trans (mul_assoc ..))

private abbrev H := M ⋊[flips] T

private theorem flips_apply (x : T) (p : M) (i : ℕ) :
    (flips x p).toAdd i = sgn (x.toAdd i) * p.toAdd i := rfl

-- Inverting just coordinate i isolates that coordinate of every invariant subgroup.
private theorem single_mem {S : Subgroup M} (hs : Stable flips S)
    {p : M} (hp : p ∈ S) (i : ℕ) : ofAdd (Finsupp.single i (p.toAdd i)) ∈ S := by
  let t : T := ofAdd (Pi.single i 1)
  have he : flips t p * p⁻¹ = ofAdd (Finsupp.single i (p.toAdd i)) := by
    apply congrArg ofAdd
    ext j
    change sgn ((Pi.single i 1 : X) j) * p.toAdd j + -p.toAdd j = _
    by_cases hij : i = j
    · subst j
      simp only [Pi.single_eq_same, Finsupp.single_eq_same]
      generalize p.toAdd i = a
      decide +revert
    · rw [Pi.single_eq_of_ne (Ne.symm hij), Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne' hij]
      simp [sgn]
  exact he ▸ S.mul_mem (hs t _ hp) (S.inv_mem hp)

private theorem middle_complemented : ComplementedLattice (Subgroup H) := by
  classical
  apply semidirect_complemented flips (elementary_complemented 2 X)
  intro D
  let active (i : ℕ) := ∃ p ∈ D, p.toAdd i ≠ 0
  let L : Subgroup M :=
    { carrier := {p | ∀ i, active i → p.toAdd i = 0}
      one_mem' := fun _ _ ↦ rfl
      mul_mem' := fun {a b} ha hb i hi ↦ by
        change a.toAdd i + b.toAdd i = 0
        simp [ha i hi, hb i hi]
      inv_mem' := fun {a} ha i hi ↦ by
        change -a.toAdd i = 0
        simp [ha i hi] }
  refine ⟨L, fun t p hp i hi ↦ ?_, Subgroup.disjoint_def.mpr ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [flips_apply, hp i hi, mul_zero]
  · intro p hd hl
    apply congrArg ofAdd
    ext i
    by_contra hn
    exact hn (hl i ⟨p, hd, hn⟩)
  · intro S hs hd hl
    apply S.eq_top_iff'.mpr
    intro p
    change ofAdd p.toAdd ∈ S
    induction p.toAdd using Finsupp.induction_linear with
    | zero => exact S.one_mem
    | add a b ha hb => exact S.mul_mem ha hb
    | single i a =>
      by_cases hi : active i
      · obtain ⟨q, hq, hqi⟩ := hi
        have h := single_mem hs (hd hq) i
        let U := AddSubgroup.toZModSubmodule 3 (AddSubgroup.toSubgroup.symm S)
        have h' : Finsupp.single i (q.toAdd i) ∈ U := h
        have hm := U.smul_mem (a / q.toAdd i) h'
        change Finsupp.single i a ∈ U
        simpa [Finsupp.smul_single, smul_eq_mul, hqi] using hm
      · apply hl
        intro j hj
        exact Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne (fun h ↦ hi (h ▸ hj))

/-! ### The action on finite-coordinate functions on the binary cube -/

private instance primeSeven : Fact (Nat.Prime 7) := ⟨by decide⟩

private abbrev K := ZMod 7

-- Finite-coordinate functions on the binary cube.
private def firstCoords (x : X) (n : ℕ) : Fin n → ZMod 2 := fun i ↦ x i

private abbrev UsesFirst (n : ℕ) (f : X → K) := f.FactorsThrough (firstCoords · n)

private theorem firstCoords_mono {x y : X} {m n : ℕ} (hm : m ≤ n)
    (h : firstCoords x n = firstCoords y n) :
    firstCoords x m = firstCoords y m := funext fun i ↦ congrFun h ⟨i, lt_of_lt_of_le i.isLt hm⟩

private theorem dep_mono {m n : ℕ} {f : X → K} (hf : UsesFirst m f) (hm : m ≤ n) : UsesFirst n f :=
  fun _ _ h ↦ hf (firstCoords_mono hm h)

private def W : Submodule K (X → K) where
  carrier := {f | ∃ n, UsesFirst n f}
  zero_mem' := ⟨0, fun _ _ _ ↦ rfl⟩
  add_mem' := by
    rintro f g ⟨m, hm⟩ ⟨n, hn⟩
    exact ⟨max m n, fun _ _ h ↦ congrArg₂ (· + ·)
      (dep_mono hm (le_max_left ..) h) (dep_mono hn (le_max_right ..) h)⟩
  smul_mem' := by
    rintro c f ⟨n, hn⟩
    exact ⟨n, fun _ _ h ↦ congrArg (c * ·) (hn h)⟩

private noncomputable def weight (p : P) (x : X) : ZMod 3 :=
  p.sum fun i a ↦ sgn (x i) * a

private theorem weight_add (p q : P) (x : X) :
    weight (p + q) x = weight p x + weight q x :=
  Finsupp.sum_add_index' (fun _ ↦ mul_zero _) (fun _ _ _ ↦ mul_add ..)

private theorem weight_single (i : ℕ) (a : ZMod 3) (x : X) :
    weight (Finsupp.single i a) x = sgn (x i) * a :=
  Finsupp.sum_single_index (mul_zero _)

private theorem weight_twist (t : X) (p : P) (x : X) :
    weight (twist t p) x = weight p (t + x) := by
  classical
  induction p using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero =>
    have h : twist t 0 = 0 := by ext; exact mul_zero _
    simp [h, weight]
  | add a b ha hb =>
    have h : twist t (a + b) = twist t a + twist t b := by ext; exact mul_add ..
    simp [h, weight_add, ha, hb]
  | single i a =>
    have h : twist t (Finsupp.single i a) = Finsupp.single i (sgn (t i) * a) := by
      ext j
      change sgn (t j) * (Finsupp.single i a) j = _
      by_cases hij : i = j
      · subst j; simp
      · rw [Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne' hij, Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne' hij, mul_zero]
    rw [h, weight_single, weight_single, Pi.add_apply, sgn_add]
    ring

private def root (a : ZMod 3) : K := 2 ^ a.val

private theorem root_add (a b : ZMod 3) : root (a + b) = root a * root b := by decide +revert

private theorem weight_dep (p : P) : ∃ n, UsesFirst n (fun x ↦ root (weight p x)) := by
  use p.support.sup id + 1
  intro x y h
  apply congrArg root
  apply Finset.sum_congr rfl
  intro i hi
  have he := congrFun h ⟨i, Nat.lt_succ_of_le (Finset.le_sup (f := id) hi)⟩
  change x i = y i at he
  exact congrArg (fun b ↦ sgn b * p i) he

private theorem shift_dep (t : X) {n : ℕ} {f : X → K} (hf : UsesFirst n f) :
    UsesFirst n (fun x ↦ f (t + x)) := fun _ _ h ↦
  hf (funext fun i ↦ congrArg (t i + ·) (congrFun h i))

private noncomputable def act (g : H) (f : W) : W :=
  ⟨fun x ↦ root (weight g.left.toAdd x) * f.val (g.right.toAdd + x), by
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := weight_dep g.left.toAdd
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := f.property
    exact ⟨max m n, fun _ _ h ↦ congrArg₂ (· * ·)
      (dep_mono hm (le_max_left ..) h)
      (dep_mono (shift_dep _ hn) (le_max_right ..) h)⟩⟩

private noncomputable def action : H →* MulAut (Multiplicative W) :=
  actionOf act
    (by intro g a b; apply Subtype.ext; funext x; exact mul_add ..)
    (by
      intro a
      apply Subtype.ext
      funext x
      change root (weight 0 x) * a.val (0 + x) = a.val x
      simp [weight, root])
    (by
      intro g h a
      apply Subtype.ext
      funext x
      change root (weight (g.left.toAdd + twist g.right.toAdd h.left.toAdd) x) *
          a.val ((g.right.toAdd + h.right.toAdd) + x) =
        root (weight g.left.toAdd x) *
          (root (weight h.left.toAdd (g.right.toAdd + x)) *
            a.val (h.right.toAdd + (g.right.toAdd + x)))
      rw [weight_add, weight_twist, root_add, mul_assoc, add_right_comm, add_comm _ h.right.toAdd])

private abbrev V := Multiplicative W

private noncomputable def functions (S : Subgroup V) : Submodule K (X → K) :=
  (AddSubgroup.toZModSubmodule 7 (AddSubgroup.toSubgroup.symm S)).map W.subtype

private theorem mem_functions (S : Subgroup V) (f : W) : f.val ∈ functions S ↔ ofAdd f ∈ S := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨g, hg, he⟩
    exact (Subtype.ext he : g = f) ▸ hg
  · exact fun hf ↦ ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩

private theorem act_mem_functions {S : Subgroup V} (g : H) (hs : ∀ v ∈ S, action g v ∈ S)
    {f : X → K} (hf : f ∈ functions S) :
    (fun x ↦ root (weight g.left.toAdd x) * f (g.right.toAdd + x)) ∈ functions S := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hf
  exact (mem_functions S (act g a)).mpr (hs (ofAdd a) ha)

private theorem translate_mem {S : Subgroup V} (hs : Stable action S) (t : X)
    {f : X → K} (hf : f ∈ functions S) : (fun x ↦ f (t + x)) ∈ functions S := by
  have h := act_mem_functions (inr (ofAdd t)) (hs _) hf
  simpa [weight, root] using h

-- A generator of M acts by 2 on one half of the cube and by 4 on the other.
-- Linear combinations of this operator and the identity give both half-cube projections.
private theorem select_formula (a b : ZMod 2) :
    (if b = 0 then 2 else 6 : K) +
      (if b = 0 then 3 else 4 : K) * root (sgn a) = if a = b then 1 else 0 := by decide +revert

private theorem select_mem {S : Subgroup V} (hs : Stable (action.comp inl) S) (i : ℕ) (b : ZMod 2)
    {f : X → K} (hf : f ∈ functions S) :
    (fun x ↦ if x i = b then f x else 0) ∈ functions S := by
  have hm := act_mem_functions (inl (ofAdd (Finsupp.single i 1))) (hs _) hf
  change (fun x ↦ root (weight (Finsupp.single i 1) x) * f (0 + x)) ∈ functions S at hm
  simp only [weight_single, mul_one, zero_add] at hm
  let c : K := if b = 0 then 2 else 6
  let d : K := if b = 0 then 3 else 4
  have he : c • f + d • (fun x ↦ root (sgn (x i)) * f x) =
      fun x ↦ if x i = b then f x else 0 := by
    funext x
    change c * f x + d * (root (sgn (x i)) * f x) = _
    rw [← mul_assoc, ← add_mul, select_formula]
    split <;> simp
  exact he ▸ (functions S).add_mem ((functions S).smul_mem c hf) ((functions S).smul_mem d hm)

private theorem select_cell {S : Subgroup V} (hs : Stable action S) (y : X)
    {f : X → K} (hf : f ∈ functions S) (n : ℕ) :
    (fun x ↦ if firstCoords x n = firstCoords y n then f x else 0) ∈ functions S := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simpa [Subsingleton.elim (firstCoords _ 0) (firstCoords y 0)] using hf
  | succ n ih =>
    convert select_mem (fun p ↦ hs (inl p)) n (y n) ih using 1
    funext x
    have he : firstCoords x (n + 1) = firstCoords y (n + 1) ↔
        firstCoords x n = firstCoords y n ∧ x n = y n := by
      constructor
      · intro h
        exact ⟨firstCoords_mono (Nat.le_succ _) h, congrFun h ⟨n, by omega⟩⟩
      · rintro ⟨h, hn⟩
        funext i
        by_cases hi : i.val < n
        · exact congrFun h ⟨i, hi⟩
        · change x i.val = y i.val
          rwa [show i.val = n by have := i.isLt; omega]
    simp only [he]
    split_ifs <;> tauto

-- A nonzero function yields an indicator on every translate of any sufficiently small cell.
private theorem cell_mem {S : Subgroup V} (hs : Stable action S) {f : X → K}
    (hf : f ∈ functions S) {y : X} (hy : f y ≠ 0) {n : ℕ} (hd : UsesFirst n f)
    (z : X) : (fun x ↦ if firstCoords x n = firstCoords z n then (1 : K) else 0) ∈
      functions S := by
  have h := select_cell hs y hf n
  have he : (f y)⁻¹ • (fun x ↦ if firstCoords x n = firstCoords y n then f x else 0) =
      fun x ↦ if firstCoords x n = firstCoords y n then (1 : K) else 0 := by
    funext x
    simp only [Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    split_ifs with hx
    · rw [hd hx, inv_mul_cancel₀ hy]
    · exact mul_zero _
  have h' := he ▸ (functions S).smul_mem (f y)⁻¹ h
  convert translate_mem hs (y - z) h' using 1
  funext x
  have hh : firstCoords (y - z + x) n = firstCoords y n ↔ firstCoords x n = firstCoords z n := by
    simp only [funext_iff, firstCoords, Pi.add_apply, Pi.sub_apply]
    exact forall_congr' fun i ↦ by constructor <;> intro hi <;> linear_combination hi
  simp only [hh]

private def extendCoords {n : ℕ} (u : Fin n → ZMod 2) : X :=
  fun i ↦ if h : i < n then u ⟨i, h⟩ else 0

private theorem firstCoords_extend {n : ℕ} (u : Fin n → ZMod 2) :
    firstCoords (extendCoords u) n = u := funext fun i ↦ dite_eq_left i.isLt

private theorem simple_action (S : Subgroup V) (hs : Stable action S) (hne : S ≠ ⊥) : S = ⊤ := by
  have h := mt S.eq_bot_iff_forall.mpr hne
  push Not at h
  obtain ⟨f, hf, h1⟩ := h
  apply S.eq_top_iff'.mpr
  intro g
  have hy : ∃ y, f.toAdd.val y ≠ 0 := by
    by_contra! ha
    apply h1
    apply congrArg ofAdd
    exact Subtype.ext (funext ha)
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hy
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := f.toAdd.property
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := g.toAdd.property
  let n := max m l
  have cells (u : Fin n → ZMod 2) :
      (fun x ↦ if firstCoords x n = u then (1 : K) else 0) ∈ functions S := by
    have h := cell_mem hs ((mem_functions S f.toAdd).mpr hf) hy
      (dep_mono hm (le_max_left m l)) (extendCoords u)
    change (fun x ↦ if firstCoords x n = firstCoords (extendCoords u) n then (1 : K) else 0) ∈
      functions S at h
    simpa only [firstCoords_extend] using h
  apply (mem_functions S g.toAdd).mp
  classical
  have he : g.toAdd.val = ∑ u : Fin n → ZMod 2, g.toAdd.val (extendCoords u) •
      (fun x ↦ if firstCoords x n = u then (1 : K) else 0) := by
    funext x
    simp only [Finset.sum_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero,
      Finset.sum_ite_eq, Finset.mem_univ, ite_true]
    apply dep_mono hl (le_max_right m l)
    exact (firstCoords_extend _).symm
  rw [he]
  exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun u _ ↦ (functions S).smul_mem _ (cells u)

/-! ### The ambient group and its normal subgroup -/

private abbrev G := V ⋊[action] H
private abbrev N := V ⋊[action.comp inl] M

private theorem ambient_complemented : ComplementedLattice (Subgroup G) := by
  apply semidirect_complemented action middle_complemented
  intro D
  by_cases h : D = ⊥
  · exact ⟨⊤, fun _ _ _ ↦ trivial, h ▸ disjoint_bot_left, fun _ _ _ hl ↦ top_unique hl⟩
  · refine ⟨⊥, ?_, disjoint_bot_right, fun S hs hd _ ↦ simple_action S hs ?_⟩
    · intro g v hv
      rw [Subgroup.mem_bot.mp hv, map_one]
      exact Subgroup.one_mem _
    · exact fun he ↦ h (bot_unique (he ▸ hd))

private noncomputable def projection : G →* T := rightHom.comp rightHom

private noncomputable def normalEquiv : N ≃* projection.ker where
  toFun g := ⟨⟨g.left, inl g.right⟩, rfl⟩
  invFun g := ⟨g.val.left, g.val.right.left⟩
  left_inv _ := rfl
  right_inv g := by
    apply Subtype.ext
    exact SemidirectProduct.ext rfl (SemidirectProduct.ext rfl g.property.symm)
  map_mul' a b := by
    apply Subtype.ext
    exact SemidirectProduct.ext rfl (map_mul inl a.right b.right)

-- Inside N the subgroup of functions vanishing at zero is normal.
private def vanishing : Subgroup V :=
  AddSubgroup.toSubgroup (((LinearMap.proj (R := K) (φ := fun _ : X ↦ K) 0).comp
    W.subtype).ker.toAddSubgroup)

private theorem stable_vanishing : Stable (action.comp inl) vanishing := by
  intro p v hv
  change root (weight p.toAdd 0) * v.toAdd.val (0 + 0) = 0
  rw [zero_add, show v.toAdd.val 0 = 0 from hv, mul_zero]

private noncomputable def obstruction : Subgroup N := pairSubgroup vanishing stable_vanishing ⊥

private theorem normal_obstruction : obstruction.Normal := by
  constructor
  intro a ha g
  obtain ⟨hl, hr⟩ : a.left ∈ vanishing ∧ a.right ∈ (⊥ : Subgroup M) := ha
  have he : a = inl a.left := SemidirectProduct.ext rfl (Subgroup.mem_bot.mp hr)
  rw [he, conj_inl]
  exact ⟨stable_vanishing _ _ hl, Subgroup.one_mem _⟩

private theorem normal_not_complemented : ¬ ComplementedLattice (Subgroup N) := by
  intro hN
  obtain ⟨B, hB⟩ := hN.exists_isCompl obstruction
  let := normal_obstruction
  have factor (g : N) : ∃ a ∈ obstruction, ∃ b ∈ B, a * b = g :=
    Subgroup.mem_sup_of_normal_left.mp (hB.sup_eq_top.ge (Subgroup.mem_top g))
  have surj : B.map rightHom = ⊤ := by
    apply (B.map rightHom).eq_top_iff'.mpr
    intro p
    obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hb, hab⟩ := factor (inr p)
    have ha' := Subgroup.mem_bot.mp (show a.right ∈ (⊥ : Subgroup M) from ha.2)
    exact ⟨b, hb, by simpa [ha'] using congrArg SemidirectProduct.right hab⟩
  let S := B.comap inl
  have hs : Stable (action.comp inl) S := stable_comap B surj
  have faithful {f : X → K} (hf : f ∈ functions S) (hz : f 0 = 0) : f = 0 := by
    obtain ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩ := hf
    have ha : inl (ofAdd v) ∈ obstruction := ⟨hz, Subgroup.one_mem _⟩
    have h1 := Subgroup.disjoint_def.mp hB.disjoint ha (show inl (ofAdd v) ∈ B from hv)
    exact congrArg (fun g : N ↦ g.left.toAdd.val) h1
  -- Factoring the constant function gives a function in the complement taking value 1 at zero.
  let oneFn : W := ⟨fun _ ↦ 1, 0, fun _ _ _ ↦ rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hb, hab⟩ := factor (inl (ofAdd oneFn))
  have ha' := Subgroup.mem_bot.mp (show a.right ∈ (⊥ : Subgroup M) from ha.2)
  have hb' : b.right = 1 := by simpa [ha'] using congrArg SemidirectProduct.right hab
  have hmem : b.left.toAdd.val ∈ functions S :=
    (mem_functions S _).mpr (show inl b.left ∈ B from
      (show inl b.left = b from SemidirectProduct.ext rfl hb'.symm) ▸ hb)
  have he : a.left * b.left = ofAdd oneFn := by
    simpa [ha'] using congrArg SemidirectProduct.left hab
  have hz : b.left.toAdd.val 0 = 1 := by
    have hh := congrArg (fun v : V ↦ v.toAdd.val 0) he
    change a.left.toAdd.val 0 + b.left.toAdd.val 0 = 1 at hh
    simpa [show a.left.toAdd.val 0 = 0 from ha.1] using hh
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := b.left.toAdd.property
  -- Cut along a coordinate outside its dependence. The result vanishes at zero but equals 1 at x.
  let x : X := Pi.single n 1
  have hx : firstCoords x n = firstCoords 0 n := by
    funext i
    exact Pi.single_eq_of_ne (Nat.ne_of_lt i.isLt) _
  have hzero := faithful (select_mem hs n 1 hmem) (by simp)
  have hx' : x n = 1 := Pi.single_eq_same ..
  have := congrFun hzero x
  simp [hx', hn hx, hz] at this

/-- **Normal subgroups of $K$-groups need not be $K$-groups.** There is a group $G$ whose subgroup
lattice is complemented (a $K$-group) with a normal subgroup $N$ whose own subgroup lattice is not
complemented; so Kourovka Problem 11.128 has a negative answer.

The Kourovka Archive answers 11.128 "No, it is not" (Obraztsov).

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved
Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 11.128 (M. Emaldi); resolution: V. N. Obraztsov, J. Austral. Math. Soc.
(Ser. A) 61, no. 2 (1996), 267-288, Kourovka Archive, Problem 11.128: "No, it is not",
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem normalSubgroupOfKGroupIsKGroup_refuted : ¬ normalSubgroupOfKGroupIsKGroup := by
  intro h
  have := h G ambient_complemented projection.ker inferInstance
  exact normal_not_complemented normalEquiv.symm.mapSubgroup.complementedLattice

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ComplementedSubgroupLatticeNormalKourovka11Problem128Wanted
